survey sanitizer

# Station Equivalences

# Survey data

# This is the streamway continuation found this Sunday.
# Station 1 is the start of the streamway (foot of climb)

# It is nearly tied into St Giles later.

centreline
  # BCRA2
  sd length 0.5 metres
  sd compass clino 2.5 degrees
  calibrate compass 4.2
  data normal from to length compass clino
  1	2	8.8	305	0
  2	3	17.4	310	0	# 3=jct straight across
  3	4	4.6	310	-25
  4	5	7.7	225	0
  5	6	5.9	170	0
  6	7	7.2	240	-5
  7	8	4.9	335	-40
  8	9	14.0	265	0	# 9=jct rt
  9	10	7.1	175	0
  10	11	4.6	130	0
  11	12	6.6	245	0
  12	13	4.7	235	-20
  13	14	4.2	240	-5
  14	15	3.1	160	0	# tape unclear - I will check
  15	16	9.3	210	0	# 15=jct left
  16	17	4.8	300	0	# 17=jct right
  17	18	8.8	215	0	# 18=jct right
  18	19	11.9	140	0
  19	20	3.1	175	-20
  20	21	6.1	205	0
  21	22	3.7	185	0
  22	23	12.4	165	0
  23	24	8.0	170	-5
  24	25	5.9	290	0
  25	26	4.8	165	0
  26	27	11.8	210	0
  27	28	9.8	295	0
  28	29	14.1	180	0	# Suspicious bearing -- reversed?
  29	30	14.6	320	0
  30	31	12.5	190	0
  31	32	5.3	260	0	# 32 = sump

  # return to climb that drops into stream
  1	33	7.6	-	up
  33	34	2.9	120	+15
  34	35	9.3	110	+10	# 35 = bolt - end of survey
  35	36	4.0	-	down	# guessed leg

  # Station 36 is a guess at the location of
  # Station 12 of the St Giles survey performed on 6 May
  # It could be miles out. Will check next time!

endcentreline
survey t
# The following survey data was carried out by James Hooper and Jenny
# Vernon (OUCC) on 4/6/'95. BCRA grade 2.

centreline
  # BCRA2
  sd length 0.5 metres
  sd compass clino 2.5 degrees
  calibrate compass 4.2
  data normal from to length compass clino
  1	2	19.5	165	0	# 1=OUCC (6/5/'95) station 13 (at start of Wiggley business)
  2	3	1.6	-	up	# 3=OUCC (28/5/'95) station 35 (bolt at start of Sanitizer

endcentreline
endsurvey

# The following is a side passage leading off the Sanitizer streamway
# named "Branch 9". We surveyed from the end back to OUCC (28/5/'95)
# station 9. The end is a slightly draughting dig.
# 
# Survey conducted:	4/6/95
# 
# Surveyed by: 		James Hooper and Jenny Vernon (OUCC).
# Compass:
# Tape:
# Clinometer:
# Book:
# 
# BCRA Survey Grade:	2
# 
# Data entry:		James Hooper, Tim Long

survey branch9

centreline
  # BCRA2
  sd length 0.5 metres
  sd compass clino 2.5 degrees
  calibrate compass 4.2
  data normal from to length compass clino
  1	2	3.9	025	0	# 1=end of "Branch 9"
  2	3	5.0	125	0	# 2=permanent survey station
  3	4	2.3	060	0
  4	5	1.8	055	0
  5	6	5.2	140	0
  6	7	2.4	130	0	# 7=OUCC (28/5/'95) station 9

endcentreline
endsurvey

# The follow is a second side passage leading off the Sanitizer
# streamway. There are several leads from this but the most interesting
# thing is a fault line rift (about 5m high) that continues wide open. We
# didn't have time to survey (or push) all of this draughting lead.
# The area has been named "The land of Mr. Ugg."
# 

survey mr_ugg

centreline
  # BCRA2
  sd length 0.5 metres
  sd compass clino 2.5 degrees
  calibrate compass 4.2
  data normal from to length compass clino
  1	2	4.2	220	0	# 1=permanent survey station (located along draughting rift at foot of small climb.
  2	3	3.2	180	0
  3	4	5.7	180	0
  4	5	2.2	165	0
  5	6	4.6	210	0
  6	7	3.5	210	0
  7	8	4.0	245	0
  8	9	6.0	265	0	# 8=permanent survey station, 9=dig
  8	10	3.9	170	0
  10	11	4.2	045	0
  11	12	5.2	035	0
  12	13	6.6	140	0
  13	14	9.6	150	0	# 14 is near OUCC (28/5/'95) station 18 in the Sanitizer streamway but we couldn't find the scratched triangle.
  14	15	8.5	040	0	# 15= OUCC (28/5/'95) station 17

endcentreline
endsurvey

endsurvey
